codex
I found a cleaner path that removes the iterator bridge entirely. I’m encoding integer lists with total selector equations (`empty`, `head`, `tail`) so `intVals` exposes a typed integer head without inverse-function reasoning. Fixed reference rules will perform every iterator step; the proof-local equations only construct the symbolic input and define its mathematical fold. This materially simplifies Gate A by eliminating all execution replacement.
apply patch
